        <headline>Hazardous Seas Warning issued September 25 at 1:48AM PDT until September 25 at 2:00PM PDT by NWS Medford OR</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Gale Warning, southwest winds 20 to 30 kt with
gusts up to 35 kt and seas 10 to 14 ft at 7 seconds expected.
For the Hazardous Seas Warning, very steep and hazardous seas 10
to 12 ft at 8 to 9 seconds expected.

* WHERE...Gale Warning north of Reedsport early this morning with
a Hazardous Seas Warning for all areas into this afternoon.

* WHEN...For the Gale Warning, until 5 AM PDT early this
morning. For the Hazardous Seas Warning, until 2 PM PDT this
afternoon.

* IMPACTS...Strong winds and very steep seas could capsize or
damage vessels. Low visibility conditions are expected.

* View the hazard area in detail at https://go.usa.gov/x6hks
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners should alter plans to avoid strong winds and very steep
seas. Remain in port, seek safe harbor, alter course, and/or
secure the vessel for severe conditions.</instruction>
